docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:14:| Law 1 — arrival determines semantic and integrity claims | CONFORMS for custody/projection authority; SILENT-DIVERGENCE for the Wave-1 agreement surface | Re-derivation and derived JSONL use arrival alone: [arrival_projection.py:252](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_projection.py:252). Arrival-native L1 agreement audit is absent: CX-DC-01. |
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:17:| Law 4 — positions compare only within one lineage | CONFORMS structurally | Cross-lineage application refuses and same-lineage foreign positions re-resolve rather than reuse rowid: [witness.py:466](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/witness.py:466). This is the r1 CX-BR-03 disposition. The coordinate itself remains wrong; see CX-DC-02. |
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:21:| §9 — witness addressing and seals re-based on arrival | SILENT-DIVERGENCE | Neither surface was re-based: CX-DC-02 and CX-DC-03. |
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:43:| §10 — seals/witness basis over arrival | SILENT-DIVERGENCE | The facts-only content rule conforms, but the selector remains rowid-based: CX-DC-03. Interleave-uniqueness vectors are correctly absent as tail work. |
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:50:| §1 — Wave 1 is slices 0+A–D, landing together | SILENT-DIVERGENCE | Branch history and receipts stop after C; the missing D obligations are CX-DC-01 through CX-DC-03. |
