docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:73:| Rewrite authority prose across store reader/witness/declaration/docs | SILENT-DIVERGENCE | Witness and audit prose still describe rowid/legacy authority: CX-DC-01 and CX-DC-02. |
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:88:### CX-DC-01 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: Wave-1 arrival agreement audit and shuffled-index gate are absent
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:92:Contradicted design sentence: “`canonical_audit.py`’s entire offset/prefix custody model moves to arrival … [and] audit vectors over a deliberately rebuilt and shuffled index” ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79), [gate](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:83)).
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:94:### CX-DC-02 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: public witness positions remain projection rowids
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:96:`WitnessPosition` stores `fact_id`, `rowid`, `seq`, lineage and store path; its prefix is `WHERE rowid <= rowid`: [witness.py:164](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/witness.py:164). Same-lineage portability is implemented by resolving the fact id to another projection’s rowid: [witness.py:471](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/witness.py:471). The r1 Law-4 fix makes misuse structural, but it does not re-key the coordinate.
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:98:Contradicted design sentences: “Its position is the witness position: `(arrival_lineage, ordinal)`” ([Substrate §3](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:92)); “witness addressing, re-keyed on `(lineage, ordinal)`” ([Substrate §9](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:471)); and Plan D’s seal/witness rebase ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79)).
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:100:### CX-DC-03 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: seals remain derived-index rowid commitments
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stdout.log:104:Contradicted design sentence: “seals, chain verification, signing — re-based on arrival positions” ([Substrate §9](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:477)); Plan D is more explicit: “Seals re-base on `(arrival_lineage, ordinal)`” ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79)).
