docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19114:01M09GNGW7VTSKDPYMJ027HEPR	design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar			RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-17 session with Fable — the slice-0 ratify gate per plan:arrival-libs-slice-0 is now OPEN for implementation). The arrival log record grammar + suffix design fact, proposal doc: docs/dev/arrival-slice0-record-grammar-2026-08-17.md (authored by a Claude design agent over an agy-explorer ledger; all citations spot-verified).\n\nCORE: suffix .arrival (companions .arrival.lock / .arrival.tmp); JSON-lines framing inheriting the ensure_ascii/allow_nan=False encoder discipline; record fields in order v, lin, ord, prev, at, k, observer, origin, body, sig?, rh; coordinate (lin, ord) WRITTEN INTO the record — append validates, never assigns; rh = sha256(JCS(record-without-rh)); prev chains rh from slice 0 (deferring to slice D would leave a permanent chain hole); torn tail truncates ONLY under the append lock, corrupt interior always refuses; genesis is ordinary record at ord=0, k=genesis, sig REQUIRED, O_EXCL staging + atomic rename + directory fsync; append under fcntl.flock on .arrival.lock (mutual exclusion forced by ordinal assignment), reads lock-free; resume mark = (arrival_lineage, arrival_offset, arrival_ordinal), all three validated, counts custody DISSOLVES. NAMED DEPARTURE, ratified as such: body is a JSON object, not verbatim TEXT — the verbatim-payload invariant retires with the two-custody-holders condition that created it; JCS defines canonical bytes.\n\nKYLE'S THREE RULINGS: (1) sig covers CONTENT ONLY (k, at, observer, origin, body — field-for-field the existing commitment envelope) — coordinate-covering signatures would make identity store-local; portable single identity across many stores is the point. Coordinate integrity rides rh/prev. (2) Genesis body MINIMAL in slice 0 — protocol version + lineage claim; document set and migration pins are slice A's, where a genesis has real history behind it. (3) Suffix .arrival over .lineage after vocabulary workshop — lineage is a PROPERTY of the records; the logs are the arrival of observations. Axis name stays continuous across filesystem, SDK (ArrivalHead), and meta keys (arrival_*).\n\nVOCABULARY: seed denylist EMBEDDED per plan:arrival-vocabulary-ratchet (jsonl_canonical + jsonl_* meta family, receipt_order/receipt_mode/receipt-as-custody, event-as-ordering, reanchor-as-operation, merge-touches-custody, rewind, mergeability/union-discipline, two-CAS-species names — the last as a pointer slice C resolves against the ruled list). Glossary ratified: arrival log, record, lineage, ordinal, coordinate, genesis, head, append, resume mark, torn tail, projection, body. Named adjacency: witness.py late_arrivals is a different (witness-time) sense; slice A decides its rename.\n\nGATE (slice-0, empirical): six tests in proposal §3.5, headlined by 4 real OS processes x 250 appends asserting dense gapless ordinals + intact prev chain + recomputing rh. Real processes, not threads — the gate is not passed otherwise.
docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19122:01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F	design/arrival-sliceC-ordering	ratified		RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-19): Cut C — ORDERING design contract. Full body: docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/design-proposal.md (committed on feat/arrival-libs). Spine: ordering is DECLARED, never inferred — atoms Ordering union Arrival()|ByKey(field) + ONE totalization beside it, every reader consumes that primitive; .arrival is the only real store, legacy families frozen byte-for-byte. Q1 totalization: ByKey sort key (K(record), record.id ASC), id NEVER semantic time (NON-NEGOTIABLE); missing-K = non-membership in the projection (Kyle-ratified posture, vector-pinned); type-mixed K REFUSES loudly (no coercion); flat payload field this cut; no lang grammar change (LensDecl key attr = later thin constructor, dissolution test). Q2 'arrival' is SINGLE-STORE-ONLY (ordinals dense per-log): aggregates must ByKey, default ByKey('ts'); aggregate+Arrival refuses loudly; _combined_read store-count fork DISSOLVES into declared ordering ("interim state" comment retires — this is the ruling it awaited); single-store Arrival ≡ old rowid sequence byte-identical (gate pin). Q3 CAS token = arrival head (record_ordinal, fact_id), batch rows share record ordinal; predicate keeps lineage-filtered _decl.*-only semantics verbatim; _INTENT_VERSION BUMPS, old intents refuse via IntentCorrupt posture; legacy declaration_head FROZEN untouched; test axis rewrite: cas-token test pins ARRIVAL apart from (ts,id); gate: token agrees with from-scratch log walk. Q4 ordered(prefix,key) on StoreReader, read-time sort, NO new index (benchmark-justified later); perf benchmark item extends to ordered() pre-ship. Q5 dissolution takes the WHOLE bridge module store/jsonl.py (_receipt_order + export_jsonl + rebuild_jsonl + ORDERING RULE docstring + tests) — exporting under substitute order would rewrite receipt history on rebuild; residue swept same change: __init__ exports, sl store export CLI arm (apps/ NOT diff-empty this cut, Kyle-ratified departure from B), refusal-message pointers merge.py:120 + jsonl_store.py:689/755, RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md R2/R3; JsonlStore engine class UNTOUCHED; planned frozen last-0.x sidecar keeps its own copy (e1: no sidecar exists yet — future home named, nothing to fence). Q6 generate_lens grows key axis against the atoms primitive; existing ts vectors become ByKey('ts') family BYTE-IDENTICAL (normative, loops-go reads them); new families: non-ts key + adversarial missing-K/mixed-type/id-tiebreak; checkpoint dispatch tests enumerate Ordering variants — Arrival licenses checkpoint+replay_from suffix, ByKey cold-folds. Q7 Rule 17 scan scope = slice C0 first commit: git ls-files selection + docs/scratch exclusion, shrink-only. KEEP (NON-NEGOTIABLE): Spec.replay_from, VertexHandle checkpoint machinery, benchmark arms, Rule 17 semantics, ArrivalStore write path (except CAS coordinate), legacy families. Commit seams C0-C5, C1→{C2,C4,C5}. GATE items 1-7 in proposal incl. main-checkout full suite post-merge.
