   412	## Gate plan
   413	
   414	Independent gate agent; re-derives the oracle from scratch; pointer branch
   415	`slice/D-gate`.
   416	
   417	**G-D0-1 — the shuffled index (the ruled gate item).** A natural rebuild
   418	*cannot* produce a shuffled index: `rederive_projections` replays in order,
   419	so it reproduces the original rowid assignment by construction. The gate
   420	therefore needs a **deliberate permuted-insert harness** — build an index by
   421	inserting `rows_of_record` output in a permuted record order, so rowid order
   422	and arrival order disagree. Assertions: L1 passes; every witness position,
   423	seal window, and audit check answers identically to the unshuffled store.
   424	Any answer that changes under permutation is a rowid dependency that
   425	survived the re-key. This harness is the slice's central artifact and should
   426	be written first.
   427	
   428	**G-D0-2** — deliberately rebuilt index (`rederive_projections`): outstanding
   429	positions and seals still valid.
   430	
   431	**G-D1-1** — `durable_handle` output byte-identical before/after the re-key.
   432	**G-D1-2** — `WitnessAggregateUnsupported` raised at all three sites with
   433	unchanged messages; A10 refusal messages unchanged. Pinning tests:
   434	`libs/engine/tests/test_witness_position.py`,
   435	`libs/engine/tests/test_diff_interval_report.py`,
   436	`libs/engine/tests/test_query_facts.py`, `libs/engine/tests/test_fold_at.py`
   437	— they match on message substrings and must pass untouched.
   438	**G-D1-3** — `seq:N` round-trip across a batch boundary, pinning whichever
   439	D1-Q1 answer Kyle rules.
   440	**G-D1-4** — same-path store-replacement refusal (the new `arrival_lineage`
   441	guard).
   442	
   443	**G-D2-1 — backward verifiability, empirically.** A fixture store sealed by
   444	the pre-D code: after the re-key, `verify_chain` is green **and** each
   445	window hash is byte-equal to the legacy computation. Not an argument, a
   446	byte comparison.
   447	**G-D2-2** — a seal spanning a batch record: window membership and hash
   448	identical before/after.
   449	**G-D2-3** — unresolvable cursor still hashes as empty.
   450	
   451	**G-D3-1** — L1 detects: index behind arrival; out-of-band sqlite insert;
   452	edit to the last consumed row. Each with the expected coordinate in the
   453	message.
   454	**G-D3-2** — L1 makes no byte-offset custody read and stays cheap: no
   455	`open(canonical, "rb")` remains on the L1 path, and L1 calls neither
   456	`ArrivalLog.read` nor `ArrivalLog.walk` (assert by construction or by
   457	counting records verified on a large healthy store).
   458	**G-D3-3** — torn arrival tail: L1 reports "behind", never "tampered" — the
   459	false-accusation property `_check_last_line`'s docstring protects.
   460	**G-D3-4** — derived `.jsonl` reordered line-for-line: set-membership audit
   461	still agrees (the whole point of set membership).
   462	
   463	**G-D4-1** (if arm 1 lands) — merge from a source with a forged record
   464	refuses; merge from a legacy source admits with an explicit no-claim.
   465	
   466	**Fence check, every package:** `git ls-files` diff confined to
   467	`libs/engine/`, `libs/store/` — plus, if D3-Q1 is ruled in, exactly the one
   468	dispatch in `apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`.
